  message: "docs-prose:F2 surfaced this but DEFERRED it for human approval. The fix is a one-line correction in a .agent/ playbook (self-analysis-dogfooding-playbook.md line 165), which states 'There is no module:name shorthand' — but the shorthand IS implemented: slice --entry accepts module:name (e.g. cli:main) per cli.py:6244-6246 help. PROPOSED CHANGE: replace the false denial with a note that the module:name shorthand is supported. AGENTS.md:256 carves out that a playbook .md is not a governance file, but the Security-Boundaries .agent/** rule is in tension and CODEOWNERS has no entry, so I am routing through the approval workflow to be safe rather than self-merge a .agent/ edit. APPROVE and I will land the one-liner in the next docs PR."  # 5c84
